{"accessed_at":"2026-11-08T05:14:56.841Z","tool":"web.run","result":"Checking your browser - reCAPTCHA (https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3101863/)\nciteturn26view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3101863/\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 3\nL0: Checking your browser before accessing pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov ...\nL1: \nL2: Click 【0†here】 if you are not automatically redirected after 5 seconds.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nN-Z-Amine™ A (C0626) - Product Information Sheet (https://www.sigmaaldrich.com/deepweb/assets/sigmaaldrich/product/documents/244/967/c0626pis.pdf)\nciteturn26view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 1; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.sigmaaldrich.com/deepweb/assets/sigmaaldrich/product/documents/244/967/c0626pis.pdf\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 57\nL0@P0: N-Z-Amine A\nL1@P0: Product Number C 0626\nL2@P0: Store at Room Temperature\nL3@P0: Product Description\nL4@P0: The average MW is approximately 250 Da. The MW\nL5@P0: distribution is 54% at 100-200 Da, 36% at 200-500 Da,\nL6@P0: and 9% at 500-1000 Da.\nL7@P0: The approximate amino acid content of this product is\nL8@P0: as follows:\nL9@P0: Amino Acid Amount (mg/g)\nL10@P0: Ala 30\nL11@P0: Arg 31\nL12@P0: Asp 67\nL13@P0: Cys 3\nL14@P0: Glu 186\nL15@P0: Gly 19\nL16@P0: His 22\nL17@P0: Ile 44\nL18@P0: Leu 75\nL19@P0: Lys 68\nL20@P0: Met 27\nL21@P0: Phe 40\nL22@P0: Pro 88\nL23@P0: Ser 51\nL24@P0: Thr 42\nL25@P0: Trp 10\nL26@P0: Tyr 28\nL27@P0: Val 59\nL28@P0: The total amino acid content is approximately\nL29@P0: 890 mg/g.\nL30@P0: This product is an enzymatic digest of casein. This\nL31@P0: product is not vitamin free. The presence of vitamins\nL32@P0: has been confirmed, but the amount was not\nL33@P0: determined. These vitamins are present in most\nL34@P0: casein enzymatic hydrolysates. It is recommended\nL35@P0: that a yeast extract be included in culture media to\nL36@P0: insure the presence of sufficient amounts of vitamins\nL37@P0: for growth of cultures. Alternatively, meat digests such\nL38@P0: as Product Nos. P 7750 or P 8388 (peptone type I and\nL39@P0: type II) can be used in place of N-Z-Amine products as\nL40@P0: a source of amino acids. The vitamin content will be\nL41@P0: higher, but it is still advisable to supplement with\nL42@P0: additional vitamins for fastidious cultures. The type of\nL43@P0: nutrient used, casein hydrolysate or meat hydrolysate,\nL44@P0: may influence the type of metabolic byproducts the\nL45@P0: cultured bacteria will produce.\nL46@P0: Precautions and Disclaimer\nL47@P0: For Laboratory Use Only. Not for drug, household or\nL48@P0: other uses.\nL49@P0: Preparation Instructions\nL50@P0: This product is soluble in water (100 mg/ml) with\nL51@P0: heating at 95 °C for 5 minutes.\nL52@P0: MWM/AJH 10/02\nL53@P0: Sigma brand products are sold through Sigma-Aldrich, Inc.\nL54@P0: Sigma-Aldrich, Inc. warrants that its products conform to the information contained in this and other Sigma-Aldrich publications. Purchaser\nL55@P0: must determine the suitability of the product(s) for their particular use. Additional terms and conditions may apply. Please see reverse side of\nL56@P0: the invoice or packing slip.\n"}
